cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use P.E.N. or its analog catalog, please cite it as below."
title: "P.E.N.: Planetary Environmental Navigator"
abstract: >-
  P.E.N. finds and schedules Earth analog sites for lunar south-pole Moon Base sites and Mars landing areas.
  It scores 6 km Earth windows at 30 m by terrain and by low-Sun cast shadows, validates its light model against
  NASA LOLA illumination maps, and reports where the analogy breaks (temperature, ice, minerals).
